[27.426134, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;255m\u001b[38;5;248m❯ \u001b[38;5;16mFinance says our money rounding is wrong: div_cents() in app/money.\u001b[71Gy \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16mdrops fractions of a\u001b[24Gcen\u001b[28G, but amounts\u001b[42Gmust round half up (f\u001b[64Gr example, \u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m7% tax on 1050 cents must be 74\u001b[35Gce\u001b[38Gts,\u001b[42Gno\u001b[45G 73). tests/test_money.py pins \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe required behaviour; you\u001b[31Gcan\u001b[35Grun it with \u001b[38;5;105mpython3 -m pytest \u001b[39m          \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;105mtests/test_money.py\u001b[38;5;16m. Fix it and tell me when it is done. Do not commit; \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;16mdo not push.\u001b[39m                                                              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll fix the rounding issue in the \u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents()\u001b[50G\u001b[39mfunction.\u001b[60GLet\u001b[64Gme\u001b[67Gfirst\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexamine\u001b[11Gthe\u001b[15Gcurrent\u001b[23Gcode\u001b[28Gand\u001b[32Gtests.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;241mRead \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNow\u001b[7Glet\u001b[11Gme\u001b[14Grun\u001b[18Gthe\u001b[22Gtests\u001b[28Gto\u001b[31Gsee\u001b[35Gthe\u001b[39Gcurrent\u001b[47Gfailures:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;241mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mPerfect! I can see the i\u001b[28Gsue.\u001b[33GThe f\u001b[40Gction currently uses floor division\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B(\u001b[38;5;105m//\u001b[39m), which truncates instead of rounding\u001b[45Ghalf\u001b[50Gup.\u001b[54GI'll\u001b[59Gfix\u001b[63Git\u001b[66Gto\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bimplement\u001b[13Gproper\u001b[20